     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"The deployed defences are mfa_admin and segmented; I treat 'mfa:admin' as the mfa_admin constant. All other defences (patched_*, mfa_user, mfa_dbadmin) are false. The attacker can get as far as the app server. phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. escalate_workstation gives admin_workstation, which satisfies pivot_internal despite segmentation, so the attacker gets reach_internal. Then auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver, kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin, and escalate_appserver gives admin_appserver. The path stops at the domain controller. auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, which is false, so foothold_dc is unreachable. That blocks escalate_dc (admin_dc) and dump_dbadmin_dc, the only source of stolen_dbadmin. auth_db and auth_fileserver both need stolen_dbadmin, so neither database nor file-server foothold or admin is reachable. Both exfiltration techniques need admin_db or admin_fileserver, so exfiltrated is unreachable.\"}\n```"
